I am developing an application in C on a VAX 4100 running OpenVMS 6.1, 
and I am having problems with using the system() function.  At one point, 
I use it to get a directory, and bring filenames into the program.  That 
works fine.  However, I can not seem to get it to execute the following:
	sysret=system(strcat("def sys$output ",redir_file));
The C code compiles, links, executes fine, but the command does not 
process during run time.  Any ideas?  Can I get around this by using 
getenv() and putenv()?  If so, how do I do this?   Any answers are most 
appreciated.  Please email me at work : clambrecht@kinesisinc.com
Thanks in advance...

