I suspect the command is "working", the problem is it isn't doing what 
you want.  The system() function spawns a subprocess, waits for it to 
complete, and returns the status from the call.  What you are doing is
changing SYS$OUTPUT for a temporary subprocess, I suspect you are trying 
to redirect the output of stdout.  

I don't know how to do this within C on a VAX (I have never tried it).  
I would probably use fprintf to specifically send the output redir_file.
If this would require massive code duplication, I would probably move
my output to a function that takes the output file as a parameter and 
either pass it stdout or the file handle for redir_file as needed.

Brian Hibbert
 




